\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Empirical illustration of the KCOR workflow on a deterministically selected grouped Czech cohort comparison (2021-07 enrollment, grouped dose 2 versus dose 0 reference). (A) The raw observed cumulative hazards differ in both level and curvature. (B) The earlier monthly normalization adjusted each cohort's hazards using the slope fitted in its quiet period. The resulting cumulative hazards are more nearly linear. (C) KCOR(t) is then computed as the cumulative contrast on that normalized scale. This figure is intended to illustrate the geometric effect of the workflow on an analysis example rather than to serve as a standalone substantive result.}}{6}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:kcor_empirical_intuition}{{1}{6}{Empirical illustration of the KCOR workflow on a deterministically selected grouped Czech cohort comparison (2021-07 enrollment, grouped dose 2 versus dose 0 reference). (A) The raw observed cumulative hazards differ in both level and curvature. (B) The earlier monthly normalization adjusted each cohort's hazards using the slope fitted in its quiet period. The resulting cumulative hazards are more nearly linear. (C) KCOR(t) is then computed as the cumulative contrast on that normalized scale. This figure is intended to illustrate the geometric effect of the workflow on an analysis example rather than to serve as a standalone substantive result}{figure.caption.14}{}}
